# Paper PDFs (large binary files — reference locally, don't push)
*.pdf

# Experiment outputs
wandb/
output/
outputs/
checkpoints/
runs/

# Old notebooks with hardcoded tokens — never commit these
prev_*_old.ipynb
*_old.ipynb

# Markdown: planning/working docs stay local (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, PlanA.md,
# future_directions.md, chen_email_draft.md, …). README.md is the one exception —
# it is the repo's front page for collaborators.
# NOTE: this rule does not affect files already tracked by git (e.g. the vendored
# transformers/**/*.md docs); those stay tracked deliberately.
*.md
!README.md
!data/**/SOURCE.md

# Task 13/14 benchmark data. Nothing here is authored by us, so none of it is committed:
#   * SWORDS, bm-semlex and HyperLex are fetched by `verify_task14_data.py --download_missing`
#     against pinned URLs and SHA-256 digests in data/external_benchmarks_manifest.json
#     (which IS tracked -- it is the pin).
#   * concept_dev/ and */youtube_clean_gold/ are regenerated byte-identically by
#     prepare_swords_concept_sets.py and rebuild_gold_inclusive.py from tracked inputs.
# SOURCE.md provenance notes are kept; the payloads are not.
data/swords/*
!data/swords/SOURCE.md
data/bm_semlex/*
!data/bm_semlex/SOURCE.md
data/hyperlex-data/*
!data/hyperlex-data/SOURCE.md
data/syn/youtube_clean_gold/
data/hyp/youtube_clean_gold/
data/youtube_clean_gold_report.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.env
.venv
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Jupyter checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/
